Read the guidance index first: [openrouter-chat-cli guidance](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat-cli/index.md). Each reference covers one area; open the ones for the paths you touch.

| Changing | Read |
| --- | --- |
| The turn loop, retries, tools, structured output, MCP | [effect-ai](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat-cli/effect-ai.md), [openrouter](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat-cli/openrouter.md) |
| Request settings, the models list, attribution | [openrouter](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat-cli/openrouter.md), `docs/openrouter.md` |
| Anything under `src/tui/` | [tui](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat-cli/tui.md), [design-slop](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat-cli/design-slop.md), `DESIGN.md` |
| Tests, fixtures, evals | [testing](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat-cli/testing.md) |
| A new command, service or tool | [workflows](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat-cli/workflows.md) |

The rules that hold everywhere:

- Use Effect AI with the OpenRouter provider. Read the installed packages' exports and type declarations before writing code, and keep what you verify in `docs/guidance/effect/api.md`.
- stdout carries only the result. `{{project_slug}} mcp` writes only JSON-RPC frames; errors go to stderr as `{"error":{tag,message,retryable}}` with `--json`.
- Only `src/tui/launch.tsx` imports Effect inside the TUI, and nothing outside `src/tui/` imports it statically. `biome-plugins/chat-boundaries.grit` flags both.
- Tests never reach the network. The only fake is the shipped stub OpenRouter in `tests/helpers/stub-openrouter.ts` (plus the release stub when bun-release is selected). Never mock the app's own modules.
- Two runners: vitest on Node for `tests/`, `bun test` for `tests/tui/`. A bare `bun test` skips every vitest test.
- `bun run eval` and `bun run record:openrouter` call the real API and cost money. They never run in tests or CI.

Before calling work done, follow [verification](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat-cli/verification.md): `bun run check`, read the counts, then drive the CLI against `bun run stub`.

The Claude-only TypeScript hooks aren't installed for this agent, so keep the same boundaries through the project linter and tests.
